        }

        #6rZbIPQGjUyu231IxpCxSt ^"Touched by Meido" DEF {
            ^"Description" STRING "Activation: When making a check pertaining to spirits, Shibito may receive 3 strife to roll 1 additional ring die and keep 1 additional die as if she had spend 1 Void point."
        }

        RULES {
            #L5REE30kaiuShibitoTsune1: kaiu_shibito_tsuneko "Kaiu Tsuneko felt constrained by her family's history. Her work didn't fit the mold, so to bolster her design decisions, she researched the history not only of Kaiu architecture, but of the ancient constructions by the beings that came before humanity. Each discovery only fueled her desire for stranger and more ancient works, and she soon abandoned her family's vocation in order to search ruins and ancient buildings.\n\nOnce merely consumed with discovering secret construction techniques, Tsuneko saw her fortunes and health take a turn for the worse after an encounter near Morikage Toshi. She refuses to discuss the event for fear of some supernatural retribution. Her family has disowned her, striking her name from the family record, but some relatives want to bring her back and cure her of her delusions.\n\nWhether deluded or inspired, \"Shibito\"—the name that villagers call her, though she responds to her given name equally well—now believes that the dead remember the details she needs about long-forgotten buildings. She spends more time with them than with the living. She appears wan and emaciated, her hair long and unkempt, and unless she comes across an offering at a grave or shrine, she often forgets to eat or drink.\n\nLittle interested in the affairs of mortal humanity, Shibito can be found talking to herself—or to the spirits, as she claims. She remains a scholar at heart, and a living person can get her talking if they can teach her something new about the spirits, architecture, history, or any craft."
        }
    }
    # --- Wilderness (Troll) ---
    # source stat block (page 221)
    #vkvg5HuwllAhJSR1LjlaeH ^"Kasai, Mournful Troll" DEF {
        EXTENDS #t4540de6f35155c46f41f0 ^"NPC"

        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Type" STRING "Adversary" FIXED
            ^"Combat Conflict Rank" INTEGER 8
            ^"Intrigue Conflict Rank" INTEGER 4
            ^"Rings" DEF {
                ^"Air" INTEGER 2
                ^"Earth" INTEGER 4
                ^"Fire" INTEGER 5
                ^"Water" INTEGER 4
                ^"Void" INTEGER 3
            }
            ^"Demeanor" STRING "Morose"
            ^"Social Skill Check TN Modifiers" STRING "Water +2, Fire -2"
            ^"Endurance" INTEGER 18
            ^"Composure" INTEGER 11
            ^"Focus" INTEGER 4
            ^"Vigilance" INTEGER 3
            ^"Honor" INTEGER 35
            ^"Glory" INTEGER 15
            ^"Status" INTEGER 5
            ^"Skills" LIST OF STRING ["Artisan 1", "Martial 3", "Scholar 6", "Social 2", "Trade 2"]
            ^"Advantages" LIST OF STRING ["Brute Strength (Air) [Martial; Physical]"]
            ^"Disadvantages" LIST OF STRING ["Pessimism (Water) [Social; Interpersonal]"]
            ^"Favored Weapons" LIST OF STRING ["Massive Cudgel: Range 2, Damage 9, Deadliness 5, Cumbersome", "Rending Grip: Range 1, Damage 4, Deadliness 6"]
            ^"Gear" LIST OF STRING ["Armor scraps and scaled hide (Physical 2, Supernatural 1)", "Stolen sake and scrolls"]
        }

        #fQeubyv1VYFjwtRsmrfdkm ^"Ancient and Powerful" DEF {
            ^"Description" STRING "Kasai is an Otherworldly being of silhouette 4."
        }

        #8kb23MMuGum0fKdCRMdifn ^"Temper" DEF {
            ^"Description" STRING "Each time Kasai suffers 1 or more fatigue, he gains 1 strife. When Kasai's strife exceeds half of his composure, he gains the Enraged condition."
        }

        #72q6VBAbTm6OdkmTHyFkjk ^"Sustaining Fury" DEF {
            ^"Description" STRING "Kasai cannot suffer the Incapacitated or Unconscious condition while he has the Enraged condition."
        }

        #jjiCmgrUSuDYCrVhhGMaVg ^"Primordial Wisdom" DEF {
            ^"Description" STRING "As a downtime activity, Kasai can share ancient secrets with characters who have earned his trust. Characters who heed this wisdom can purchase the Channel the Fire Dragon kiho technique regardless of prerequisites."
        }

        RULES {
            #L5REE30kL0mN2oP4qR6sT8uV: kasai_troll "This troll, who calls himself \"Kasai,\" has lost so many members of his people that he has retired to the Valley of Spirits to get away from humans. He bears the scars, physically and emotionally, of centuries watching his people disappear into the Shadowlands, die by natural causes, or get killed by humans. Tall, but hunched over from age, every scar on his body and long, gangly arms comes with a story, a history lesson, of the betrayals and violence of the human race.\n\nYet, despite his misanthropy, he has refrained from deliberately killing humans. In the Valley of Spirits, he attacks intruders to drive them away, dressed in rags to appear as a spirit. He howls in the dark of night to frighten travelers, and he sometimes leaves animal carcasses to rot both to scare humans and to chase them away with the stench. He calls himself a base animal—assuming anyone can get close enough to listen—but continues to cling to civilization. He keeps the scrolls and books he finds on human corpses or dropped by frightened travelers. He takes stones and fallen wood to build structures throughout the forest. And if a wanderer listens closely, they can hear low, guttural singing, terrible and lonely throughout the night.\n\nHe wants to seek out more of his kind, but that requires him to make a long overland journey through human lands. His hatred of humans wars against his self-discipline; he refuses to turn into a monster and cut a bloody path home. So, he keeps himself in isolation."
        }
    }

    # --- Coastal Waters (Pirate) ---

    # source stat block (page 226)
    #oKuscc2DmcQRL2Wi6cpbbL ^"Uranaishi no Manami, Ambitious Pirate" DEF {
        EXTENDS #t4540de6f35155c46f41f0 ^"NPC"

        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Type" STRING "Adversary" FIXED
            ^"Combat Conflict Rank" INTEGER 4
            ^"Intrigue Conflict Rank" INTEGER 2
            ^"Rings" DEF {
                ^"Air" INTEGER 2
                ^"Earth" INTEGER 1
                ^"Fire" INTEGER 3
                ^"Water" INTEGER 4
                ^"Void" INTEGER 2
            }
            ^"Demeanor" STRING "Shrewd"
            ^"Social Skill Check TN Modifiers" STRING "Water +2, Fire -2"
            ^"Endurance" INTEGER 10
            ^"Composure" INTEGER 8
            ^"Focus" INTEGER 5
            ^"Vigilance" INTEGER 3
            ^"Honor" INTEGER 45
            ^"Glory" INTEGER 65
            ^"Status" INTEGER 30
            ^"Skills" LIST OF STRING ["Artisan 1", "Martial 4", "Scholar 2", "Social 3", "Trade 3"]
            ^"Advantages" LIST OF STRING ["Keen Sight (Water) [Trade; Physical]"]
            ^"Disadvantages" LIST OF STRING ["Bluntness (Air) [Social; Interpersonal]"]
            ^"Favored Weapons" LIST OF STRING ["Katana: Range 1, Damage 4, Deadliness 5/7, Ceremonial, Concealable, Razor-edged"]
            ^"Gear" LIST OF STRING ["Concealed armor (Physical 2, Concealable)", "Wakizashi", "Sake jug", "well-thumbed book on history, etiquette, or courtly romance"]
        }

        #wk43Dq3vVrL9OWr0o9YVyn ^"Dirty Tricks" DEF {
            ^"Description" STRING "When performing an Attack action check, Manami may spend (op) in the following way:\n\n(op)+: One character at range 0-2 suffers the Disoriented condition."
        }

        RULES {
            #L5REE31wX1yZ3aB5cD7eF9gH: manami_pirate "The Mantis consider Manami one of their best pirates, but she hates her reputation and that of her clan, wishing she could be seen as a legitimate samurai. Torn between three impulses—to live a simple life of fishing and seafaring, to provide for her family and clan with continued raids, and to obtain the recognition and respect of the other clans—Manami leads her crew with a shrewd grumpiness. She chooses a single wealthy target over several smaller, easier ones to avoid as much bloodshed as possible. If she is challenged on a decision, she solves the disciplinary problem with some grappling, and her short, stocky, powerful body quickly proves her physical might. Her successful piracy count demonstrates her significant tactical insight.\n\nWhen the tsunami hit Crane lands, instead of picking at the corpses and villages like carrion, Manami rescued several survivors. Informing her sailors that the Crane may pay a ransom for their people, she has treated these outsiders well, integrating them at a village near Toshi no Inazuma. This scheme has not paid off and may be an unflattering mark on her record, but her sailors remain loyal and well fed from their work, so they don't complain.\n\nThe Mantis Clan, however, has mixed feelings about this act of mercy, and especially about taking on responsibility for people loyal to the Crane; some doubt her dedication to piracy and to the Mantis.\n\nThose jealous of her success and popularity continually bring up this softening in her heart. What they truly fear is her ambition. She has openly discussed sending tribute and representatives to Otosan Uchi to turn the Mantis into a Major Clan. With each successful raid, the possibility becomes more real, with her name on top of the list to represent the Mantis."
        }
    }
}
